cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OralScale: scalable, privacy-preserving oral assessment"
message: "If you use this software or its design in your teaching or research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Inouye
    given-names: David
    name-particle: I.
    website: "https://www.davidinouye.com"
    affiliation: "Purdue University"
abstract: >-
  OralScale delivers oral assessment at scale using a static web application and a
  stateless edge signer, with a learning-management system as the system of record.
  A cryptographic certificate establishes that an answer was spoken live, without
  sending audio anywhere but the system of record, and grading runs locally by
  default so that student work does not leave the institution's boundary.
keywords:
  - oral assessment
  - academic integrity
  - engineering education
  - privacy-preserving assessment
  - automated grading
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0-alpha.1
repository-code: "https://github.com/inouye-lab/oralscale"
